SUMMARY:Friday Nights at OMCA with Shanté | Nexus Black Art Week
LOCATION:Oakland Museum\, 1000 Oak St\, Oakland\, CA 94607
DESCRIPTION:Live Music by Shanté\, Music Set by DJ Moteef\, Drag Storytime
  with Per Sia\, Mini House Making\, Nexus Black Art Week Panel Discussion\
 , and Gallery Chats This Friday Night at OMCA\, Oakland singer-songwriter 
 Shanté brings her soulful sound to the Garden Stage with a powerful live 
 performance. Blending smooth R&B\, heartfelt storytelling\, and uplifting 
 messages of resilience\, faith\, and self-discovery\, the East Oakland art
 ist delivers an intimate yet energetic set that invites audiences to sing 
 along\, reflect\, and leave inspired.\nhttps://museumca.org/event/friday-n
 ights-at-omca-with-shante/\nFrom Pushpin Bay Area: https://pushpin.city/ba
 yarea/
URL:https://museumca.org/event/friday-nights-at-omca-with-shante/
END:VEVENT
